**File:** `server/src/service/infrastructure/networkService.js` **Lines ~210-220**

```javascript
// Priority: exactIdMatch || exactNameMatch || partialIdMatch
let targetContainer = exactIdMatch || exactNameMatch || partialIdMatch;

// Ambiguous check only across TYPES, not within same type
const matchTypes = [];
if (exactIdMatch) matchTypes.push("exact ID");
if (exactNameMatch) matchTypes.push("exact name");
if (partialIdMatch && !exactIdMatch) matchTypes.push("partial ID");

if (matchTypes.length > 1) { /* warn */ }
```

**Misses ambiguity within same type**: Two containers with same name (different namespaces?) or two containers where short ID prefix matches both. `partialIdMatch` uses `.find()` (first match) silently. Should check `containers.filter(c => c.Id.startsWith(normalizedInput)).length > 1`.

